// Both previously read from the wrong semantic alias — `--zimm-color-bg-05` and
// `--zimm-color-opacity-40` happened to LOOK plausible (the active one even resolves to
// the identical hex, since bg-05 and border-focus both trace to the same grey/900
// primitive) but were never actually confirmed against the design, per this file's own
// prior comment. Now confirmed via `get_design_context`: the active segment is Figma's
// `border/focus` token; every other segment is `border/secondary` — a flat, opaque light
// grey, notably lighter than the semi-transparent overlay `opacity-40` previously
// produced. Both are already-registered tokens, not new ones.
background: isActive ? 'var(--zimm-color-border-focus)' : 'var(--zimm-color-border-secondary)',

